{"tool_name":"medecom","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"medecom","home":"http://public.genetik.uni-sb.de/medecom/","summary":"Computational method for decomposition of heterogeneous DNA methylomes. It applies matrix factorization with biologically motivated constratints and regularization to discover and quantify latent components in methylomes of multi-cellual samples.","addition_date":"2016-06-02T14:29:19Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:52Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["0.2"],"collections":["HD-HuB","de.NBI"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:medecom","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"p.lutsik@dkfz-heidelberg.de","name":"Pavlo Lutsik","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://public.genetik.uni-sb.de/medecom/"},{"name":"Martin Slawski","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Pavlo Lutsik","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"hdhub","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Hein Lab","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"],"url":"http://www.ml.uni-saarland.de/people/hein.htm"},{"name":"Walter lab","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"],"url":"http://epigenetik.uni-saarland.de/de/home/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/lutsik/MeDeCom/blob/master/README"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["Karl_JV"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Statistical inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3658"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"PNG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3603"},{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]},{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"R file format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3554"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"MeDeCom","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"hdhub","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-017-1182-6","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 The Author(s).It is important for large-scale epigenomic studies to determine and explore the nature of hidden confounding variation, most importantly cell composition. We developed MeDeCom as a novel reference-free computational framework that allows the decomposition of complex DNA methylomes into latent methylation components and their proportions in each sample. MeDeCom is based on constrained non-negative matrix factorization with a new biologically motivated regularization function. It accurately recovers cell-type-specific latent methylation components and their proportions. MeDeCom is a new unsupervised tool for the exploratory study of the major sources of methylation variation, which should lead to a deeper understanding and better biological interpretation.","authors":[{"name":"Gasparoni G."},{"name":"Hein M."},{"name":"Lutsik P."},{"name":"Slawski M."},{"name":"Vedeneev N."},{"name":"Walter J."}],"citationCount":33,"date":"2017-03-24T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"MeDeCom: Discovery and quantification of latent components of heterogeneous methylomes"},"pmcid":"PMC5366155","pmid":"28340624","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Epigenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3295"},{"term":"Microarray experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MeDeCom","home":"https://bio.tools/medecom","version":"0.2","summary":"Computational method for decomposition of heterogeneous DNA methylomes. It applies matrix factorization with biologically motivated constratints and regularization to discover and quantify latent components i